# Generated previews (level maps, wave transects, ride strips, gameplay
# screenshots) — tooling output, regenerated on demand with `make level` /
# `make waves` / `make ride` / `make screenshots`.
#
# ANCHORED to the root on purpose. Unanchored, this pattern matches a
# directory called `previews` at any depth — including a pwa/public/previews/
# the campaign menu will one day ship its banners from.
/previews/

# Recorded runs (`make record`, once it exists) — a ride is somebody's own
# measurement, not repository content.
runs/

# Release scratch
.release-notes.md

# THE PLATFORM SHELLS. `native/` (the store app) is built and carries a
# .gitignore of its own — its dependency tree, its prebuilt ios/ and android/
# projects, the packed webroot.zip, its .env and every piece of signing
# material. `tauri/` (the desktop app) is still a placeholder, a README and
# nothing else; when it arrives it brings the same set. Nothing in either may
# be a personal identifier or a credential in a committed file.

# Store submission OUTPUT. The authored source is native/store/listing.mts;
# everything below is regenerated by `make store-metadata`, and gitignored for
# the reason pwa/dist is: reviewing a generated listing in a pull request helps
# nobody.
#
# THE LISTING'S OWN WORDS. A description, subtitle, promo text and keyword set
# are what the store indexes and what a competitor reads, so publishing them
# puts the listing's own prose on a crawlable page under somebody else's
# domain. The RULES stay committed (native/store/listing.mts), a SKELETON
# documents the shape (copy.example.mts), and the words are not here. Nothing
# backs this file up: keep a copy outside the checkout.
native/store/copy.mts

native/store/store.config.json
native/store/screenshots/
native/fastlane/metadata/
